CHAPTER.VERS:
Are we beginning again to commend ourselves? Or do we need, as do some, letters of commendation to you

          {+}
         or from you

          {+}
        ?

Our letter is you

          {+}
        , written in our hearts, known and read by all men;

being made manifest that you

          {+}
         are a letter of Christ, served by us, not written with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tables of stone, but in tables [that are] hearts of flesh.
